// ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
// Customary COMMERCIAL real estate closing costs, by state — transfer taxes, title,
// recording. GENERATED by the transfer-tax research pipeline (9/24/26 overhaul);
// state-level lines here, local tables in ./transferTaxLocal/, engine in
// ./closingCostEngine.ts.
//
// THE RULES (Eric, 9/24/26):
//   • Every rate line carries its own SOURCE and AS-OF date (a test fails the
//     build otherwise — __tests__/transferTaxSources.test.ts).
//   • Every state declares the LEVEL where local transfer taxes are set
//     (none / county / municipality / municipality+school / county+municipality),
//     with a citation — including for "no local tax".
//   • The estimate is right for the EXACT locality or it says it can't verify it:
//     a county/town not in the local table is shown as a RANGE with a red banner,
//     never a silent default.
//   • `ratesAsOf` = when the state's rates were last checked against the sources;
//     the card warns once that is more than 12 months old (annual refresh).
//   • KPR Transfer Tax Answer Key v01 (__tests__/fixtures) must match within
//     0.001 percentage points on every row.
//
// WHO PAYS: customary splits per Fidelity National Title "Laws & Customs by State"
// (and the statutes/ordinances cited on each line). Customary splits are
// negotiable per deal — confirm with the title company and counsel.
// ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
